CVE-2026-123633: use-after-free in HTTP/2 stream creation (nginx.org: critical,
CVSS 4.0 9.2, unauthenticated remote code execution; fixed in 1.31.9 / 1.30.7).

An HTTP/2 connection could be marked reusable while it already had streams.  A
connection with no streams and a partial frame read from the client is
registered as reusable (to limit DoS), and the reusable status was not reset
when the remaining bytes arrived and a stream was created.  While processing
that stream (for example when connecting to an upstream) the connection could be
drained, a GOAWAY send attempted, and on send failure the connection closed and
its pool released, which triggers a use-after-free further up the stack.  The
bug needs HTTP/2 enabled and, for this CVE, a config that proxies to an upstream.

Backport of upstream nginx commit 0c87dd1db413 ("HTTP/2: reset reusable
connection status on stream creation"), cherry-picked with no functional
changes (only hunk offsets differ against the patched 1.27.1 base):
https://github.com/nginx/nginx/commit/0c87dd1db413e440a4e3ef7ee8acc518509e8809

The fix is one line: ngx_reusable_connection(h2c->connection, 0) in
ngx_http_v2_create_stream().

Why this applies to this build: the behaviour was introduced upstream by
76672e650 ("HTTP/2: reuse of connections with incomplete frames", Feb 2021,
nginx 1.19.7), which is an ancestor of 1.27.1, so the vulnerable code is present.

Compatibility: only the body of ngx_http_v2_create_stream() changes.  No header,
struct layout, public symbol or directive is touched, so there is no ABI impact
for third-party modules.

Reported upstream by Albert of Vexera AI.

diff --git a/src/http/v2/ngx_http_v2.c b/src/http/v2/ngx_http_v2.c
index bea5c88eae..e0e7ef379b 100644
--- a/src/http/v2/ngx_http_v2.c
+++ b/src/http/v2/ngx_http_v2.c
@@ -3109,6 +3109,8 @@ ngx_http_v2_create_stream(ngx_http_v2_connection_t *h2c)
 
     h2c->processing++;
 
+    ngx_reusable_connection(h2c->connection, 0);
+
     h2c->priority_limit += h2scf->concurrent_streams;
 
     if (h2c->connection->read->timer_set) {
CVE-2026-123007: HTTP/2 flow control window overflow leading to memory
corruption (nginx.org: critical, CVSS 4.0 9.2, unauthenticated remote code
execution; fixed in 1.31.9 / 1.30.7).

When a stream is terminated, its unsent payload length is refunded to the
connection flow control window.  If the client had raised the window with
WINDOW_UPDATE after the stream frames were queued and before the stream was
terminated, the refund could push the window past NGX_HTTP_V2_MAX_WINDOW.  That
breaks the buffer size control in ngx_http_v2_send_chain(), which leads to
memory corruption and a possible crash or worse.  HTTP/2 must be enabled.

Backport of upstream nginx commit b89c4100bf67 ("HTTP/2: account for queued
frames when validating WINDOW_UPDATE"), cherry-picked with no functional
changes (only hunk offsets differ against the patched 1.27.1 base):
https://github.com/nginx/nginx/commit/b89c4100bf6762a45e4a6463eaf4b70368277c94

The fix tracks queued-but-unsent frame bytes in a new h2c->send_queued counter
(incremented in ngx_http_v2_send_chain(), decremented when a DATA frame is sent
and when a stream is cleaned up) and counts it when validating a client
WINDOW_UPDATE, as the client sees queued frames as part of the window.

Why this applies to this build: the refund logic dates back to nginx 1.9.5
(2015) per the public write-up, so it is present in 1.27.1.

Compatibility (ABI): this patch adds a field, send_queued, to
ngx_http_v2_connection_s in ngx_http_v2.h, which changes the struct layout.
Third-party dynamic modules built against stock nginx that touch the HTTP/2
connection struct may need rebuilding.  The build compiles every module it
ships (NDK, set-misc, headers-more, lua) from source in the same build, so
nothing shipped in the image is affected.  No directive or public symbol changes.

Reported upstream by Xint.io.

diff --git a/src/http/v2/ngx_http_v2.c b/src/http/v2/ngx_http_v2.c
index e0e7ef379b..e5d93733f0 100644
--- a/src/http/v2/ngx_http_v2.c
+++ b/src/http/v2/ngx_http_v2.c
@@ -2484,13 +2484,13 @@ ngx_http_v2_state_window_update(ngx_http_v2_connection_t *h2c, u_char *pos,
         return ngx_http_v2_state_complete(h2c, pos, end);
     }
 
-    if (window > NGX_HTTP_V2_MAX_WINDOW - h2c->send_window) {
+    if (window > NGX_HTTP_V2_MAX_WINDOW - h2c->send_window - h2c->send_queued) {
         ngx_log_error(NGX_LOG_INFO, h2c->connection->log, 0,
                       "client violated connection flow control: "
                       "received WINDOW_UPDATE frame "
                       "with window increment %uz "
                       "not allowed for window %uz",
-                      window, h2c->send_window);
+                      window, h2c->send_window + h2c->send_queued);
 
         return ngx_http_v2_connection_error(h2c, NGX_HTTP_V2_FLOW_CTRL_ERROR);
     }
