CVE-2026-121810: HTTP/3 (QUIC) use-after-free when worker_connections run out
(reported by Xint.io, disclosed 2026-11-18 as part of "NGINX2Root"; fixed in
nginx 1.31.9 / 1.30.7).

nginx changes (1.30.7): "use-after-free might occur in a worker process when
using HTTP/3 if worker_connections were not enough".

ngx_quic_create_stream() cleared the main connection's reusable flag and then
called ngx_get_connection() before inserting the new stream into the stream
tree.  If the worker was low on free connections, the drain inside
ngx_get_connection() could close an idle stream of the same main connection.
With the new stream not yet in the tree, that close found no streams left and
marked the main connection reusable again, so it could later be drained and
freed while one of its streams was still in use (for example while connecting
to an upstream).  The fix inserts the stream into the tree before calling
ngx_get_connection() and removes it again on the error paths.

Backport of upstream nginx commit b5252dae1 ("QUIC: avoid main connection
reuse after creating a stream"); its stable-1.30 cherry-pick c58d2a22d is
identical.  Applied with no functional changes (only hunk offsets differ
against the patched 1.27.1 base):
https://github.com/nginx/nginx/commit/b5252dae1ca0d4c516b8bcffd9fa7fd967b73075

Reachability in ingress-nginx: the controller template has no QUIC/HTTP3
listener, so this is only reachable if a "listen ... quic" is added through a
snippet.  The QUIC code is compiled in (--with-http_v3_module).  Included for
defense in depth, as with patches 43 and 44.

Compatibility: src/event/quic only; no public header, struct layout, symbol or
directive change, so no ABI impact for third-party modules.

