CVE-2026-120967: stream client SSL certificates verified against the default
server instead of the SNI-selected server (reported by CERT.PL; fixed in nginx
1.31.9 / 1.30.7).

nginx changes (1.30.7): "in the stream module, an attacker who is able to
complete the SSL handshake synchronously might cause client SSL certificates
to be verified using the configuration of the default server rather than the
virtual server selected by SNI".

If the SSL handshake completed in the first call of ngx_stream_ssl_handler(),
the client certificate was verified with the ngx_stream_ssl_module
configuration read before the handshake, which is that of the default server,
not the one selected by SNI during the handshake.  The problem was introduced
by upstream d21675228 (nginx 1.25.5), which is present in 1.27.1.  The fix
re-reads the server configuration before verifying the client certificate.

Backport of upstream nginx commit 6f9fceed8 ("Stream: client SSL certificates
were not checked with SNI"); its stable-1.30 cherry-pick 77f90f1c0 is
identical.  Applied with no functional changes (only hunk offsets differ
against the patched 1.27.1 base):
https://github.com/nginx/nginx/commit/6f9fceed8dd7eb7d39b3930dc4f6824ecfe88559

Reachability in ingress-nginx: not with the default template.  The stream
servers it generates for tcp-services and udp-services are plain TCP/UDP
proxies without "ssl", and SSL passthrough is done by the controller's own Go
